What:		/proc/task_overload/abnormal_task
Date:		2022
Contact:	OPLUS scheduler and power-management maintainers
Description:
		Reports third-party tasks that have sustained high utilization on
		the maximum-capacity CPU cluster while that cluster is at its
		maximum frequency and the middle cluster has spare capacity. Each
		record contains pid, uid, limiting state, command name and time.

		Writing the exact string FINISH_READ clears the bounded report.
		ColorOS power-stats/MIDAS userspace consumes this interface.

What:		/proc/task_overload/skip_goplus_enabled
Date:		2022
Contact:	OPLUS scheduler and power-management maintainers
Description:
		Read/write control for donor GOPLUS abnormal-task placement. Zero
		keeps monitoring and reporting active without restricting CPU
		placement. A nonzero value also prevents qualifying non-UX tasks
		from continuing to occupy the maximum-capacity cluster.

